    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. There is only one concrete test class (`AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the idempotent-create rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), the sole handler for `POST /api/owners`.\n\nThe `addOwner` operation is generated from `openapi.yml` and its signature doesn't carry the header, so I read the `Idempotency-Key` directly from the injected `HttpServletRequest`:\n\n- Added an `HttpServletRequest` constructor dependency and a small `idempotencyKey()` helper that returns the header value (or `null` when absent/blank).\n- Added a `ConcurrentHashMap<String, OwnerDto>` that remembers the owner produced under each seen key.\n- In `addOwner`: if the key was seen before, the originally created owner is returned with **200 OK** \u2014 short-circuiting before the create/validation logic (which would otherwise reject the repeat with a 409 household-duplicate conflict). Otherwise the owner is created as before (**201 Created**) and the resulting DTO is recorded under the key.\n\nThis satisfies the spec: a first create with a key returns 2xx (201), and a repeat with the same key returns the same owner id with 200 rather than creating a duplicate. Requests without the header behave exactly as before.",
