    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:203`), which calls `clinicService.saveOwner` for the only DB write. Note that despite standard Spring conventions, almost all logic lives in the **controller**, not the service, and most validation runs **outside any transaction**.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Security & pre-body checks\n\n1. **Authorization**: `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 non-admins get 403 before the method runs.\n2. **Bean Validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` (via `@Valid` + `@Validated`), before the method body. Failure \u2192 HTTP 400:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Pattern(^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit**: if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, returns the cached prior response with HTTP 200 \u2014 nothing else runs, nothing is created.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Build & validate (`buildOwnerToCreate`)\n\n4. **Side-effect \u2014 Address canonicalization** (`resolveAddressFields`): prefers `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, normalizes (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE), composes the flat `address`, and writes it back onto the DTO.\n5. **Side-effect \u2014 DTO\u2192entity mapping** via MapStruct `ownerMapper.toOwner` (ignores `id`, `pets`).\n6. **Validation \u2014 Required fields** (`validateRequiredFields`): `firstName`, `lastName`, resolved `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n7. **Validation \u2014 Postcode/region** (`validatePostcode`): if present, must be 4 digits **and** fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city allows any) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n8. **Validation + side-effect \u2014 Telephone**: normalized to E.164 (`+61` assumed, strips separators, drops leading 0), must match `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` and national-length rule \u2192 else 400. Normalized value set on entity.\n9. **Validation + side-effect \u2014 Email**: if present, must match email pattern; lower-cased; domain must not be a disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 else 400. Normalized value set.\n10. **Validation \u2014 Registration date** (`validateRegistrationDate`): if present, may not be in the future \u2192 else 400.\n11. **Side-effect \u2014 Default registrationDate** to `LocalDate.now()` if absent.\n12. **Side-effect \u2014 Business-day roll-forward**: `registrationDate` advanced past weekends and 2026 public holidays. *(Note: this happens before the limit checks below, which then measure against the adjusted date, not the client's.)*\n13. **Side-effect \u2014 householdId** derived (SHA-256 of last name + postcode) and set.\n14. **Side-effect \u2014 identityKey** set = `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + householdId`.\n15. **Validation \u2014 Household duplicate** (`rejectHouseholdDuplicate`, only when `sharesHousehold != true`): scans all non-deleted owners; matching `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n16. **Side-effect \u2014 Soft duplicate flagging** (`findPossibleDuplicate`, when not sharing household and postcode present): finds lowest-id owner with same last name + postcode + different phone; **does not reject** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` on the entity.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Enforce create limits (`enforceCreateLimits`)\n\n17. **Validation \u2014 City capacity**: if city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `OwnerCityFullException` (409).\n18. **Validation \u2014 Daily capacity**: if \u2265 100 owners share the (adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitException` (429).\n19. Computes **bulkSignupWarning** = (daily count > 80) for the response flag.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Finalize (`finalizeOwnerForCreate`)\n\n20. **Side-effect \u2014 customerCode**: `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), de-duplicated against existing codes by appending `-<n>`.\n21. **Side-effect \u2014 namesakeCount**: set to count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n22. **Side-effect \u2014 householdSize**: set to existing household members + 1.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Persist & respond\n\n23. **Side-effect \u2014 DB insert**: `clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` inside `@Transactional` (the only transactional boundary). Id via `@GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)`. No cascade child entities are created (pets never populated).\n24. **Side-effect \u2014 Audit log**: dedicated `\"AUDIT\"` logger records id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n25. **Side-effect \u2014 Response DTO derivation** (MapStruct `toOwnerDto`): computes response-only fields \u2014 `selfLink`, `salutation`, `displayName`, `initials`, Luhn `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `telephoneDisplay`, `ageBand` (not persisted).\n26. **Side-effect \u2014 Location header** set to `/api/owners/{id}`; `bulkSignupWarning` flag set on the body.\n27. **Side-effect \u2014 Idempotency store write**: response body cached under the idempotency key (in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap`).\n28. Returns **HTTP 201 Created**.\n\n**Things notably *not* done:** no email/notification sending, no password encoding, no `ApplicationEventPublisher` events, no cache eviction, and no JPA `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners` callbacks anywhere.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the read-based validations (household/city/daily/namesake scans) all run **outside** the transaction and each independently calls `findAllOwners()`, so a single create triggers many full-table scans and the duplicate/limit checks are subject to race conditions between concurrent requests."
  },
